Description: Drop the python3-future dependency
 python3-future was removed from Debian after bookworm and has no installation
 candidate on trixie, which leaves this package uninstallable on Parrot 7.x
 (apt: "Depends: python3-future but it is not installable").
 .
 The dependency is over-broad. 63 files import "builtins", but none of them need
 the future package: builtins is a Python 3 standard library module and future
 only supplies it as a Python 2 backport. Only four files genuinely used future,
 for two Python 2 shims:
 .
   * future.utils.iteritems(d)                 -> d.items()
   * future.standard_library.install_aliases() -> a no-op on Python 3
 .
 future is declared in three separate places, and all three must be cleared or
 dh_python3 and any PEP 517 build will keep requiring it:
 .
   * setup.py install_requires
   * pyproject.toml [build-system] requires
   * requirements.txt
 .
 Removing them leaves runtime behaviour unchanged on Python 3. Verified with
 future absent: import pymavlink, mavutil, the ardupilotmega dialect and message
 construction all work on Python 3.13; only the code generator was affected.
 .
 Note that bumping to current upstream is NOT an alternative fix here: pymavlink
 2.4.49 drops future but adds fastcrc, which has no Debian source package at all.
Author: Nate Jones <njones920@gmail.com>
Bug-Parrot: python3-pymavlink and rfcat uninstallable on Parrot 7.x
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-08-26
